var FDF=[{q:"Do you design and build, or only one of them?",a:"Both, and that is the point. I design the interface and then write the front-end that ships it, so nothing is lost explaining intent to a third party."},{q:"Which stack do you work in?",a:"Whatever the project already runs — commonly React, Next.js, Vue and plain semantic HTML/CSS. Design systems work is framework-agnostic: tokens and components are generated for the targets a team actually uses."},{q:"Can you work with our existing design system?",a:"Yes. I audit what exists, separate what is real from what has drifted, and either extend it or rebuild the token layer so Figma and production agree again."},{q:"How do you handle accessibility?",a:"Semantic structure, keyboard paths, focus states, contrast and reduced-motion support are part of the build. Accessibility checks run before handover, not after a complaint."},{q:"What about performance?",a:"Performance is a design constraint. I keep payloads small, images right-sized, motion cheap and pages fast on the mid-range Android devices most South African audiences use."},{q:"Do we get the code?",a:"Yes — full handover. A documented repository, component documentation and a walkthrough so your team can maintain it without me."}];
